---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import { vonar } from '../data/vonar';

const contact = 'xami.sound@gmail.com';
---

<Page
  title="Legal – privacy and terms · Xami"
  description="Privacy notice and terms of use for the Xami website and its free plugins and presets."
  eyebrow="Legal"
  heading="Privacy and terms."
  headingMuted="In plain words."
>
  <p>Last updated: 14 November 2026.</p>

  <section class="card-block" aria-labelledby="privacy">
    <h2 id="privacy">Privacy</h2>

    <h3>Who is responsible</h3>
    <p>
      The controller of this website is Xami, contact: <a href={`mailto:${contact}`}>{contact}</a>. The name and
      address of the responsible person will be provided on a justified request.
    </p>

    <h3>What is processed and why</h3>
    <p>
      This site is a set of static pages with no accounts, forms or comments. When you open a page, the hosting
      provider, Cloudflare, processes your IP address and technical details of the request (such as the page
      requested, the time and your browser's user agent). This is needed to deliver the site to you and to keep it
      secure, for example to block attacks.
    </p>
    <p>
      The legal basis is our legitimate interest in running a working and secure website (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR). You
      do not have to provide any data, but without your IP address the site cannot be delivered to your browser.
    </p>

    <h3>Statistics</h3>
    <p>This site does not use any analytics or visitor statistics tools.</p>

    <h3>Cookies</h3>
    <p>
      This site does not use cookies or similar technologies. Nothing is stored on your device, and the audio
      player does not remember any settings.
    </p>

    <h3>Who receives the data</h3>
    <p>
      Cloudflare, Inc. hosts this site and processes the data on our behalf as a processor. Cloudflare may process
      data in the United States. Transfers are based on the EU-U.S. Data Privacy Framework, under which Cloudflare
      is certified, and additionally on the standard contractual clauses in Cloudflare's data processing addendum.
    </p>
    <p>
      Download buttons lead to files hosted on GitHub. When you download a file or follow a link to GitHub, GitHub
      processes your data as a separate controller under its own privacy statement.
    </p>

    <h3>How long</h3>
    <p>Request data is kept only as long as set out in Cloudflare's policies for its services. We do not keep any copy.</p>

    <h3>Your rights</h3>
    <p>
      You have the right to access your data, to have it corrected or erased, to restrict its processing and to
      object to it on grounds relating to your particular situation. To use these rights, write to{' '}
      <a href={`mailto:${contact}`}>{contact}</a>. You also have the right to lodge a complaint with the
      supervisory authority, the President of the Personal Data Protection Office (Prezes Urzędu Ochrony Danych
      Osobowych, ul. Stawki 2, 00-193 Warszawa, Poland).
    </p>
    <p>No automated decision-making or profiling takes place.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="card-block" aria-labelledby="terms">
    <h2 id="terms">Terms</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>All plugins and presets on this site are free. No account or payment is needed.</li>
      <li>
        They are provided “as is”, without any warranty. Use them at your own risk. See sections 15 and 16 of the
        licence.
      </li>
      <li>
        Vonar is free software under the GNU Affero General Public License, version 3 (<a href={vonar.licenseUrl}
          >LICENSE</a
        >). The music and sounds you make with it are yours.
      </li>
      <li>
        The name “Vonar” and its logo are not covered by the licence. Distribute modified versions under a different
        name and logo.
      </li>
      <li>VST is a trademark of Steinberg Media Technologies GmbH.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</Page>
